  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d5e33c67f312fe45b88b04a3aece7bb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LanternKeeper.StoryNote
  noteId: Note3_Farmhands
  title: Chalked on a slate by the gate
  body: 'Here rest the hands who worked this farm: Amos, Silas, Old Bertie and the rest.


    They mean no harm. They drift toward a light the way a moth does, and they forget their manners when they get close. Raise your lantern high and bright and they''ll shy off like startled hens.


    Just don''t hold it there. A flare eats a candle whole, and they can see it from clear across the yard.'
  readRange: 1.9
